      "order": 3,
      "chapterNumber": 3,
      "headline": "The Insanity of Anger",
      "keyInsight": "Anger promises you raw power, but it secretly robs you blind. When you get furious, your brain tricks you into feeling like a fierce warrior. You puff up your chest and speak with booming thunder. But step back and look at the scoreboard. Did screaming at your slow computer make the processor run faster? Did kicking the stubborn lawnmower fix the spark plug? No, it only gave you a bruised toe and an expensive repair bill. Anger operates like drinking poison while hoping your enemy gets sick. It feels like tough justice in the moment, but it is actually pure nonsense in action.",
      "content": "Imagine you are building a wooden bookshelf in your garage. You accidentally hit your thumb with a heavy hammer. Pain shoots up your arm. What happens next? Many people drop the tool, curse at the wood, and kick the table across the floor. Now look at the room with clear eyes. Has the pain vanished from your thumb? Not at all. Is the shelf finished? No. Now you have a dented wall and a broken table to clean up too. That is the crazy math of destructive anger.\n\nAnger always sells itself as a useful weapon. It whispers that intimidation will make the world behave. If you yell loud enough at the restaurant server, your soup will arrive steaming hot. But anger always carries hidden interest rates. People might move quickly out of fear, but they will quietly resent you. Trust evaporates in your home. Colleagues stop sharing honest thoughts with you. You end up isolated on an island of your own making.\n\nEven worse, explosive fury attacks your own biological hardware. When you simmer with rage, your heart pumps fast and your stomach churns out acid. You lose restful sleep and drain your mental batteries. You cannot think clearly when your head is full of smoke. Taking the steering wheel back means trading tantrums for clear assertiveness. You can speak up firmly and solve real problems without setting your own house on fire.",
